1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:07,420
(This round is hopeless)

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,950
(Suspecting Ke's identity)
This mole means he's fake, right?

4
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,870
Okay, no problem.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,350
How about this?

6
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,470
(Defending himself weakly)
Let's just vote now.

7
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:14,300
Okay.

8
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,120
(Found a useful clue)
This is the black one, right?

9
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,290
Sure.

10
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:16,870
No problem.

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,190
Or we could just
put me on the guillotine now.

12
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,030
Fine. You can all be my executioners.

13
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:22,620
How about it?

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:23,380
(Not really okay)

15
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:24,470
Sir.

16
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,750
(Look me in the eyes)
Is this how much you trust me, sir?

17
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,670
Bro, this round...

18
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,000
This is...

19
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,310
this is a real black-box game.

20
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,380
(Actually out of ideas)

21
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:34,630
It's fine!

22
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:37,450
I don't care about pressure, okay?

23
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,320
Bring it on.

24
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:41,390
(Feeling the pressure)
That's a lot of pressure.

25
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,030
What's going on?

26
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,230
No, it's because of this...

27
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,260
I wasn't...

28
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,400
Where's yours?

29
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,270
Show me again.

30
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:47,710
No.

31
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:48,620
(Be careful)
You're destroying the evidence.

32
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,820
(Ke is out of ideas)

33
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:51,750
Alright, let's go.

34
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:55,400
You can't play like this.
What's that supposed to mean?

35
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,310
(I'm losing it)
You blame me, I can't clear my name.

36
00:00:58,310 --> 00:00:59,750
No, the most important thing is,

37
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:02,160
I restored this outfit, bro.

38
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:04,240
You know what I mean?

39
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:04,850
No.

40
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:06,400
You have to restore it.

41
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,150
If you don't restore it,
something's wrong.

42
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:08,400
You're saying if I don't restore it,

43
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,510
then it has to be him, right?

44
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:10,750
(Someone save me)
Save me.

45
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:12,300
The moment I came in,

46
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,820
I walked in and got
a fully upgraded team.

47
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:15,340
They're all coming at me.

48
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:17,560
(I really have no idea anymore)
This is insane.

49
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:19,130
Watch yourself today.

50
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:20,810
You're highly suspicious right now.

51
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:23,820
(The familiar plot unfolds again)

52
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,270
I want to see if there's anything
to check in.

53
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:25,700
There's something to it.

54
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:26,790
This key.

55
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:28,120
There's another one.

56
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,420
The cup spilled again.

57
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:36,150
(Such a familiar sight)
The cup spilled again.

58
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,990
Let's do this.

59
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,910
I think this might interfere
with our investigation.

60
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,470
This could interfere with us.

61
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,270
Starting with you, bro.

62
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,740
(Where it all began)
It starts with you.

63
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,180
(I've had enough coffee)

64
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,660
(My bubbles)

65
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,990
(Empty)
Mine is called

66
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,510
Spilled Cup.

67
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:54,380
(Spilled Cup)

68
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,630
The cup spilled.

69
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:03,630
I spilled it by accident.

70
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:05,410
(It had everyone laughing)
I accidentally knocked over the cup.

71
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:06,990
I spilled it by accident.

72
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,190
I was trying to create an effect,

73
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,710
but it got a little too dramatic.

74
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,150
(Maximum effect)
What's this supposed to be?

75
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,750
It's fine. The cup spilled earlier.

76
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,390
The cup spilled.

77
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:17,100
We were destined to spill cups today.

78
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,820
(I'm free!)

79
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:20,980
(Everyone retraces what happened,
revealing the missing key)

80
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,070
(Key missing)
My key is gone.

81
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,030
My key's missing.

82
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,460
My key is gone.

83
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,590
You left your key there to scan.

84
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:27,870
Remember?

85
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,200
You took it out when you
scanned your meal card.

86
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:29,420
Right.

87
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,310
(Perfectly recalling what happened)
You were there.

88
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,830
You pressed it against that.

89
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,590
Then I asked why you pressed it there.

90
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:35,220
(Going to look)

91
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,630
Did you pick up that key?

92
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,830
Impossible.

93
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,470
You picked up the key?

94
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,350
Did you find a key?

95
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,140
It was yours.

96
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,220
(Focused on finding the key)

97
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,260
Your name tag fell out too.

98
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,220
(He's key)

99
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:45,870
It's his.

100
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,670
I kept asking whose key it was.

101
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,090
What else could this key be?

102
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:50,930
(Just missed it)
What is this key?

103
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:51,590
He Yiwei, come back.

104
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,230
Come back.

105
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,470
Found it. I found it for you.

106
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,180
(Here it is)

107
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,110
I'm so pissed.

108
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,940
You two really are best bros.

109
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:58,860
You really are.

110
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:01,620
(A special kind of fate)

111
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:03,780
(Time to recap,
today was pure deduction)

112
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,150
(The killer, Ning Bubble, won)
You had a lot of great moments today.

113
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,830
(Ke Coffee, Ding Pudding voted right)
You pieced the case together.

114
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,870
(Ning starts praising)
They brought up the clues,

115
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,110
(He Yiwei, Jin Cardashian, Qian voted wrong)
They raised the clues.

116
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:10,990
(Allowed to be proud)
And you and Ding both caught on.

117
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,230
The two of you both caught it.

118
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,630
(As expected of me)
What did he catch first?

119
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:14,750
Liu Lian Wangfan.

120
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,550
(So satisfying)
But you connected the whole logic.

121
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,070
It was actually pretty tough.

122
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,590
(Highlight of the day)
All of this has to make the cut.

123
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,910
(It's settled)
If you cut this, I'm done for.

124
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:20,990
(See the bonus footage)
Of course.

125
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,830
Because I won, after all.

126
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,030
I have to praise everyone.

127
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,230
Qian Jinding was great too.

128
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,430
(Ning won't stop praising)
She walked in and called me out.

129
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,030
(See Truth Clubhouse for details)
Who looks most like the killer?

130
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:30,630
You.

131
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:34,830
Let me tell you,

132
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,870
this always happens
when I'm not the detective.

133
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:38,220
I was terrified.

134
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:38,980
(Sweating bullets)

135
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:40,830
I was absolutely terrified.

136
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,110
I'm telling you,

137
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,430
Ding may not know this yet.

138
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:46,110
(He's detective notes)
Ning has a very obvious tell

139
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,430
when he's the killer.

140
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,830
The first thing is, he barely talks.

141
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:52,190
(Listening intently)
He gets really calm.

142
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,670
But today, Ning was really

143
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,510
way too relaxed later on.

144
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,590
(I know what you mean)
It was impossible to find an opening.

145
00:03:58,660 --> 00:03:59,940
(Untouchable)

146
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,910
I actually suspected
him halfway through.

147
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:04,270
Because if he were innocent,

148
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,510
he'd be working really hard
to find clues.

149
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,590
But halfway through today,

150
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,510
(I was wrong)
he didn't.

151
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,550
No, because there just weren't
any clues today.

152
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,380
(Deduction mode)
Today was all about deduction.

153
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:13,270
Today was all about deduction.

154
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,030
There were no clues.

155
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,430
Unlike our last case,

156
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,270
where we'd find something

157
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,310
and run wild with theories.

158
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,270
We need to think outside the box.

159
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,590
Today was really just about...

160
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,070
Since we each know our own methods,

161
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,550
(Reasoning it out)
pure logic.

162
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,630
There weren't any clues today.

163
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,790
Get our imaginations going.

164
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,270
Yeah, exactly.

165
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:26,990
Okay.

166
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:30,220
(Jin and He's usual sibling antics)

167
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,510
What's the secret on your phone?

168
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,590
(He the foodie)
Why should I show you?

169
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,070
I paid for this video myself.

170
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,790
Hey, you, stop eating.

171
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,670
How hungry are you?

172
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,260
(Caught red-handed)

173
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,030
What's going on?

174
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,110
You ate the whole can.

175
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:46,310
Can't you buy something
to eat in Hengdian?

176
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:49,110
(I mean, seriously?)
You came here hungry just to eat?

177
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:51,220
(Coming over to see the evidence)

178
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:55,220
It's suspicious how eager you are
to find the killer.

179
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,020
(Those sharp eyes don't miss a thing)

180
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,070
He Yiwei.

181
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,990
(Looking for a tool)
That's right. Come on.

182
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,150
Hurry up.

183
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,310
(The bossy sis)
The biggest eater should get moving.

184
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:05,300
(The obedient bro)

185
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:07,550
Wow, this is fancy.

186
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:08,350
Come here.

187
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,510
Look.

188
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,830
There's a special spot for this.

189
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:13,310
You've never seen one before.

190
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,710
You've seen it?

191
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,430
(I don't buy it)
Seriously?

192
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,030
(Just being honest)
You're putting on an act.

193
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,270
(Tearing open a snack bag)
This guy's starving.

194
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:24,500
(Representing my tummy:
I'm taking you down)

195
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,700
(Jin getting serious)

196
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:28,900
(Sneaky...)

197
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:30,140
(What's that?)

198
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,180
(Who?)

199
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:32,540
(So it was you)

200
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:35,710
He Yiwei.

201
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,950
(Move aside)
Move, will you?

202
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,500
(Obediently moves away)
I'm checking the next cabinet.

203
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:43,110
I think there must
be a clue on this shirt.

204
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,830
There must be a crucial lead.

205
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,110
Let's take another close look.

206
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,270
(Hand it over)
This is my crucial lead.

207
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,620
(Sneaking around)

208
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,420
Nobody touch it.

209
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:53,820
(It's all mine)
Nobody look at it either.

210
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:54,830
Go do something else.

211
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,790
(He's got a review)
You look like a laundry-stealing creep.

212
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:00,300
(Completely focused)

213
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:01,910
(Jin's savage comment)
Eat something.

214
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,670
You'll get stupid otherwise.

215
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,790
I think it looks like a cube.

216
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:07,510
(Harsh)
I'll give you a whack.

217
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,110
Let's see if it's the same.

218
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,910
So it's this one.

219
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:10,270
Okay.

220
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:10,750
Then what?

221
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:11,230
The comment.

222
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:11,910
It proves...

223
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:12,990
Look, you've got it all over your hand.

224
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,070
Go clean it up.

225
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,430
=The Truth (Season 4)=

226
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:19,770
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at 12PM.)

227
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:20,900
(VIP updates next day at 12PM,
one week early.)
